# overpay: recorded by the port from this script (no cheats, so format 4, which DOS replays),
# from the saved game setup/trader writes; its golden is DOS's replay of that recording.
# "Journey Onward" and slot I (the player facing Brawnclan with 40 rubies in the pack); talk
# mode (F2) and the right button on him; answers 3 ("an adventurer") and 2 (trade); the rubies
# dragged out of the pack, "Move how many?" answered 40, and the left button on the first of
# the player's trade slots (twice: the first click ends the prompt); the left button on the
# first of his slots, which selects his item; then 3, the player's appraisal (do_judgement),
# and 1, the offer (do_offer). The rubies are worth 25 * 40 * 40 / 64 = 625 to the port before
# its fix, and his item a few, so the gain is far above his greed and he took them; DOS works
# it out in 16 bits, values the rubies below 0 and refuses ("No, I do not like this deal.").
# Last, 4: no more bartering
9000 key esc
12000 key enter        # Journey Onward
15000 key enter        # slot I
22000 key f2           # talk
22500 move 165 95
22700 mdown 165 95 right
22850 mup 165 95 right
26000 key 3            # "I am an adventurer in search of fortune."
29000 key 2            # "I would like to trade items with thee."
32000 move 247 88      # the rubies, dragged out of the first slot of the pack
32500 mdown 247 88 left
32800 move 230 70
33200 mup 230 70 left
34500 key backspace    # "Move how many? 1": 40
34800 key 2
35100 key 6
35500 key enter
36500 move 156 20      # the player's first trade slot, twice
36700 mdown 156 20 left
36900 mup 156 20 left
37500 mdown 156 20 left
37700 mup 156 20 left
38500 move 101 20      # his first trade slot: select its item
38700 mdown 101 20 left
38900 mup 101 20 left
40000 key 3            # "Excuse me, I must think about this deal." (the appraisal)
44000 key 1            # "I make thee this offer."
48000 key 4            # "I do not wish to barter any further."
